From 9667afd62012d69d47e3cac074d738d69bf9d6c5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Joeri Van Dooren <ure@on6ure.be>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] app: a connection through ARDOP or VARA HF switches the
 radio's modem (OpenX6X00)

The radio runs one modem at a time on its audio: ARDOP (ardopcf), or
Mercury or XARA, which Pat reaches as VARA HF, the one chosen on the
radio's Winlink page. A connection through Pat's other transport went
nowhere: the user had to change the modem on that page first (#296).

Connect() now runs the switch command the radio's supervisor names in
OPENX6X00_MODEM_SWITCH (itself, x6100-winlink) before it sets up the
TNC for an ardop or varahf connection: `<command> switch ardop|varahf`
makes the radio run a modem for that transport, waits until it is
ready, and answers bw=<Hz> for VARA HF, the bandwidth set on the radio
for the modem that runs, which the config read at Pat's start may not
have; a connection's own bw= stays. When it exits 1 nothing is dialed;
it put its reason into Pat's log, and its stderr's last line goes there
too. One switch at a time, and none while a connection through the
other transport is under way. Without the variable, and for every
other transport, Connect() is as upstream.

Not Pat's prehook: that runs once the connection is up, too late to
choose the modem, and only for a URL that names it.

With a test (app/radio_modem_test.go, with a stand-in switch).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
